    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "AAAAXn///7o\u003d",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/spi.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 110,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000187
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-05-01T19:09:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This represents a small fraction of the total cycles in the loop; timestamp_expired() and the deadline.val check (which is true only the first time through the loop) are equally large.\n\nBenchmark, THEN optimize.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAAXX//v+0\u003d",
      "revId": "7a35f4c6af4d357ba42192d2e2b4e79be4f59d22",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "AAAAXn//+ns\u003d",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/spi.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 110,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000294
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-05-02T12:42:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well this code was the result of benchmarking, and testing on a scope :-) It certainly was profiled pretty carefully. Previously I had the gpio_level_level() call but I found that it introduced a lag of several bytes.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAAXn///7o\u003d",
      "revId": "7a35f4c6af4d357ba42192d2e2b4e79be4f59d22",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "AAAAXn//+dw\u003d",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/spi.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 110,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000187
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-05-02T16:00:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we\u0027re that latency-sensitive, we probably should directly own the NSS I/O and interrupt, rather than going through the gpio layer at all.  That\u0027s what I did for one-wire communication on LM4.  \n\nSPI1_NSS is on EXTI4, so we can dedicate the EXTI4 interrupt to the SPI port and chop out another dozen clocks.\n\nHow about I detail all this in a \"profile the SPI interface\" bug and deal with it in a follow-up CL?",
      "parentUuid": "AAAAXn//+ns\u003d",
      "revId": "7a35f4c6af4d357ba42192d2e2b4e79be4f59d22",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "AAAAXn//+do\u003d",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/spi.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 112,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000187
      },
      "writtenOn": "2013-05-02T16:00:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You could buy an instruction here by putting this check *inside* if(timestamp_expired()).  That is:\n\nif timestamp expired:\n\n  if no deadline, this is the first time through the loop; set deadline\n\n  else we really have a deadline, and we\u0027ve missed it.\n\nAlso, since the only place we use DMA on STM32L is for SPI, there may be room to optimize that too.",
      "revId": "7a35f4c6af4d357ba42192d2e2b4e79be4f59d22",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
